From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msctf: context properties (1531)

ITfContext::GetProperty was E_NOTIMPL. Windows gives a property for any
GUID, made on first use and the same object after (ITfProperty): its values
are spans of the document set with SetValue/SetValueStore and read with
GetValue (VT_EMPTY where none is set), FindRange (S_FALSE where none) and
EnumRanges, and Clear cuts them, splitting a span it falls inside.

Since 1661 Word's text store context reports its edits; Word then asks for
a property, and on E_NOTIMPL it went on with nothing and faulted (in
mso20win32client) a moment later -- typing in a new document, saving and
opening the print preview restarted Word with "/restore". Spans keep their
character positions; they do not follow later edits.

Gate: test/tsfprops-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/tsfprops-probe.c).
Mutant: SG_MUTANT_NO_CONTEXT_PROPERTY (msctf/context.c).
msctf inputprocessor conformance: 285 tests, no failures, as before;
test/tsfsinks-gate.sh still passes.

